    story: Miguel Rainwraith was born in a canal boat family, where floods, ferries,
      and rope work taught respect for timing. As a child, Miguel Rainwraith lived
      through the animal cage chores, learning masks, timing, falls, applause, and
      public courage. As a young adult, Miguel Rainwraith worked through a blood
      sport contract, discovering that pain becomes easier to bear when a crowd gives
      it a price. They enter the dojo to turn a first taste of applause into real
      prize money.
